      "writeup": "A historic plantation site linked to the abolition of slavery in the islands.",
      "wiki": {
        "extract": "Sundy is a settlement in the northwestern part of Pr\u00edncipe Island in S\u00e3o Tom\u00e9 and Pr\u00edncipe. Its population is 416. Sundy lies 5 km northwest of the island capital of Santo Ant\u00f3nio. In 1822 the first cocoa plantation of the whole archipelago was established in Sundy. Several buildings of this plantation have been preserved.",
